# BUGS

C++ has no exceptions (6f2a), and no wide characters: llvm-libc's wide functions do not yet cover what libc++'s build asks for.

`std::filesystem` has no hard links (`create_hard_link` fails with `errc::not_supported`; VectraOS has symbolic links only), no `space` (no server says how much room it has), and a `hard_link_count` of 1; `last_write_time` sets the modification time alone, and a time before 1970 is refused.

`strerror` calls a known error such as `EINVAL` "Unknown error 22": llvm-libc's message table for these targets is a gap to look into.

`freopen`, `fgetpos`, `fsetpos`, `rewind`, `tmpfile` and `tmpnam` are missing: llvm-libc has none of them for any target.
`fopen`'s `"x"` (exclusive creation) is not taken.
